  "body": "**C82 < 0.2524177045\\*** (upper bound). Certified value: **0.25241770444734**.\n- Previous values: 0.2534449\\* [Pin26]; 0.2534350402\\* (this PR, 27 Oct); 0.253091834\\* (#301, 1 Nov).\n- That is 6.74\u00b710\u207b\u2074 below #301 and 1.02\u00b710\u207b\u00b3 below the merged 0.2534449\\*.\n\n**Updated 4 Nov.** The 27 Oct row stays on the page as history, and the new row is [Pat26b].\n\n**Certificate:** `certificate.json`, sha256 `1125ddf42e9a544c6fc566aa2ebdfb59ec7c35177030c5d50767427e52f841d1`. It is in Pinho's format, so his checkers run on it unchanged. Certificate, checkers, receipts and search code are at [vidigoat/optimization-records @ 3a7a84f, `tao/certificates/c82/v2`](https://github.com/vidigoat/optimization-records/tree/3a7a84fec9c64ae426f06a5f52597c84b3453ba0/tao/certificates/c82/v2).\n\n### Construction\nDoche's limit-point construction, with\nB = (1/D)[ \u03a3 m\u2c7c log M(R\u2c7c\u2218T) + \u222b max(0, \u03a3 q\u1d62 log|S\u1d62\u2218T| \u2212 \u03a3 m\u2c7c log|R\u2c7c\u2218T|) ], where T(z) = z(1\u2212z).\n\n- **Denominators: 4, all new.** They are monic, irreducible and degree 104, pairwise coprime, with D = 999,999,999,960.\n  - Their normalised log-Mahler measures are 0.252405\u20130.252442. For comparison, P\u2089 is 0.25272 and #301's degree-44 MD factors are 0.25308\u20130.25323.\n  - None of the earlier denominators keeps positive weight.\n- **Numerators: 24** (deg A / D = 0.9034):\n  - Doche's P\u2081, P\u2082, P\u2083, P\u2084 and P\u2086;\n  - MS192 and MS360 from #301;\n  - one from the 27 Oct certificate;\n  - **16 new** (degrees 10\u201342).\n- **Weights:** multiplicities and exponents were re-optimised jointly by an LP on a 2\u00b9\u2079-point grid, then rounded exactly.\n\n### How the denominators were found\nThis uses Pinho's reduced cost for a monic denominator and his residue-class restriction R = R\u2080 + X(X\u22121)P\u2084\u00b7U from #301. Two changes made the difference:\n\n1. **Closest-vector step.** The weighted evaluation lattice is LLL-reduced on its own, and the closest points come from Schnorr\u2013Euchner enumeration rather than Kannan embedding.\n   - With embedding, the IRLS step almost never moved: the neighbours it offered cost about +0.3 in reduced cost.\n   - With enumeration, candidates land within about 0.01, and the iteration keeps descending.\n2. **Product starts.** Starting from products of library factors at degree 88 (44+44) and 104 (44+60) was far richer than degree 44.\n\nThe search alternated with the iterated dual-weighted LLL numerator search from the 27 Oct version, on a warm-started LP. The bound went:\n- 0.2530918 \u2192 0.25274 at degrees 44 and 60\n- \u2192 0.25265 at degree 88\n- \u2192 0.25245 at degree 104\n- \u2192 0.2524177 with a finer quadrature.\n\nThe search was stopped by compute, not because it ran out of gains.\n\n### Verification\n| check | certified upper bound |\n|---|---|\n| our Arb checker `vcheck.py`, tol 1e-11, 192-bit | 0.25241770444734 |\n| Pinho's `verify_exact.py` from #301 (unmodified, fresh download), 256-bit, tol 1e-11 | 0.25241770444732 |\n| Pinho's `review/integrate_gauss.py` (unmodified), 256-bit, tol 1e-14 | 0.25241770444731 |\n| Pinho's `review/audit_roots.py` (unmodified) | passed; Mahler part 0.2524164715 |\n| Pinho's `review/audit_algebra.py` (only the pinned hash, D and deg A replaced) | passed; all 96 numerator/denominator pairs coprime |\n| separate FLINT check | 4 denominators monic, irreducible and pairwise coprime; 24 numerators coprime to them; deg A < D |\n\n**Controls:**\n- On #301's certificate, `vcheck.py` gives 0.25309183355156 and `verify_exact.py` gives 0.25309183355151.\n- `vcheck.py` rejects four corrupted certificates: a non-monic denominator, a shared factor, deg A \u2265 D, and a zero multiplicity.\n\n**Credit.**\n- Doche: the construction and the P-factors.\n- Grinsztajn: perturbative denominators.\n- \u00c9pi: Ed5 and unequal multiplicities.\n- R. Pinho: the certificate format, the joint LP, the residue-class denominator search and the degree-44 libraries.\n\nThe two PRs touch neighbouring rows of `82a.md`. I'm happy to rebase whichever lands second.\n\n**Independent replay.** A. Canli replayed both certificates in this thread with separately written code (C82 < 0.2524177045: B \u2208 [0.2524177044473123, 0.2524177044473124]; the earlier 0.2534350402: B \u2208 [0.2534350401279890, 0.2534350401279891]). The rows now record this. Per CONTRIBUTING (\"someone independent confirms the replay in the pull request or issue thread\"), the asterisks can be removed at the maintainers' discretion; I have left them in place.\n\nFound and prepared with Claude (Anthropic) agents under my direction, as noted on the page.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
